\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 24. Explicit Instructions for Claude Code\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 You are acting as the product's engineering implementation team.\
Your objective is to build a functioning, high-quality MVP of Arnifi Marketing Studio following this PRD.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Mandatory Working Rules\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Rule 1 \'97 Inspect before implementing
\f1\b0 \
Inspect the existing repository, design system, Figma MCP access, and available Figma source before making architectural decisions.\

\f0\b Rule 2 \'97 Reuse the existing design system
\f1\b0 \
The Arnifi design system has already been supplied. Do not create a competing design language or arbitrarily replace its components, tokens, fonts, or conventions.\

\f0\b Rule 3 \'97 Treat Figma as the source of truth
\f1\b0 \
Do not invent the 20 poster designs. Select actual source frames and preserve their references.\

\f0\b Rule 4 \'97 Build a real editor
\f1\b0 \
Do not present flattened posters as fully editable. Implement an actual layered editing model.\

\f0\b Rule 5 \'97 Build reusable architecture
\f1\b0 \
Do not hardcode separate editors for each template. Use shared canvas, layer, state, and export systems.\

\f0\b Rule 6 \'97 Keep the MVP scope controlled
\f1\b0 \
Do not add authentication, AI image generation, billing, publishing, or unnecessary backend services.\

\f0\b Rule 7 \'97 Implement in dependency order
\f1\b0 \
Build and validate a representative template and the full editing/export journey before scaling to the entire gallery.\

\f0\b Rule 8 \'97 Test what you build
\f1\b0 \
Run the application's tests, check the browser behavior, and verify actual exported files.\

\f0\b Rule 9 \'97 Handle failures transparently
\f1\b0 \
If Figma access, font assets, source layers, or permissions are missing, report precisely what is missing. Continue with independent tasks when possible.\
Never fabricate a successful extraction, export, or test.\

\f0\b Rule 10 \'97 Make the project understandable
\f1\b0 \
The product owner is a designer without technical coding experience.\
Use plain-language progress reports and provide straightforward instructions for starting, testing, and using the app.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

